/*
==============================================================================
  PoC 08 -- a refuted [reuse] lemma makes Tamarin contradict itself in one run
==============================================================================

  CLASS      : missed attack (false "verified") AND false "no trace found"
  SEVERITY   : high
  AFFECTS    : tamarin-prover 1.12.0 and develop HEAD (1.13.0)

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  WHY THIS IS THE SHARPEST RESULT IN THE SET
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Every other PoC here needs the reader to accept an argument about what the
  right answer is.  This one does not.  In a SINGLE run, on a SINGLE theory,
  Tamarin prints both of these lines:

    helper (all-traces): falsified - found trace (3 steps)
    live   (exists-trace): falsified - no trace found (2 steps)

  `helper` is  All k #i #j. Secret(k)@i & KU(k)@j ==> F
  `live`   is  Ex  k #i #j. Secret(k)@i & KU(k)@j

  "falsified" on `helper` means: THERE IS a trace with Secret(k) and KU(k).
  "falsified" on `live`   means: THERE IS NO trace with Secret(k) and KU(k).

  These are the same statement.  Tamarin asserts and denies it in the same
  summary block.  No ground truth, no modelling judgement, and no reading of
  the protocol is required to see that one of them is wrong.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  ROOT CAUSE
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  `gatherReusableLemmas` (lib/theory/src/CloseRule.hs:181-188) admits a
  [reuse] lemma on the basis of its attribute, trace quantifier, source kind
  and hide-list.  It never checks whether the lemma was proved:

      gatherReusableLemmas kind = do
          LemmaItem lem <- previousItems
          guard $    lemmaSourceKind lem <= kind
                  && ReuseLemma `elem` L.get lAttributes lem
                  && AllTraces == L.get lTraceQuantifier lem
                  && L.get lName lem `notElem` L.get pcHiddenLemmas ctxt
                  && "ALL" `notElem` L.get pcHiddenLemmas ctxt
          return $ formulaToGuarded_ $ L.get lFormula lem

  The admitted formulas are inserted via `insertLemmas` into `sLemmas`
  (CloseRule.hs:179).  `sLemmas` constrains the constraint system for BOTH
  trace quantifiers, so a false assumption does not merely close all-traces
  branches that should stay open -- it also prunes the witness search for
  exists-trace lemmas, producing "no trace found" for traces that exist.

  We verified there is no proof-status gate anywhere on this path:
  `CompleteProof` is consumed only in src/Web/Theory.hs, for colouring cells
  in the interactive GUI.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  GROUND TRUTH (for completeness -- not needed for the argument above)
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Rule Gen outputs the fresh key k directly with Out(k), so the adversary
  learns it.  `helper` and `target` are FALSE and `live` is TRUE.
  Correct verdicts: helper falsified, target falsified, live verified.
  See 08b_reuse_control.spthy, which is this theory with [reuse] removed and
  which produces exactly those three correct verdicts.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  TAMARIN SAYS
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    helper (all-traces):   falsified - found trace (3 steps)
    target (all-traces):   verified (2 steps)              <-- WRONG
    live   (exists-trace): falsified - no trace found (2 steps)   <-- WRONG

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  NOTE ON INVALIDATION
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tamarin has a proof status for exactly this hazard -- `InvalidatedProof`,
  documented in lib/theory/src/Theory/Proof.hs:406 as "The proof has been
  Invalidated (eg. by editing a reuse lemma)".  The constructor is only ever
  SET in src/Web/Handler.hs:255, i.e. in the interactive web GUI.

  The manual documents this invalidation in its interactive-mode section
  (manual/src/007_property-specification.md:229-234), so batch mode never
  promised it.  The observation is therefore not "a safety net that fails to
  fire" but "the safety net exists only in the GUI, and batch mode -- which
  is what CI and published artifacts use -- has no equivalent".
==============================================================================
*/

theory ReusePoisonsBothDirections begin

rule Gen: [ Fr(k) ] --[ Secret(k) ]-> [ Out(k) ]

// FALSE: Gen publishes k, so the adversary knows it.
lemma helper [reuse]:
  "All k #i #j. Secret(k) @ i & KU(k) @ j ==> F"

// FALSE, but "proved" from the refuted helper.
lemma target:
  "All k #i. Secret(k) @ i ==> not(Ex #j. KU(k) @ j)"

// TRUE, but reported "no trace found" because the refuted helper is asserted
// into sLemmas for the witness search too.
lemma live: exists-trace
  "Ex k #i #j. Secret(k) @ i & KU(k) @ j"

end
